# BlueMap map configuration — template values to merge.
# Destination on the server: <instance-data>/plugins/BlueMap/maps/<map-id>.conf
# Example map IDs: world, world_the_nether, world_the_end.
#
# BlueMap writes a file per map on first boot. Stop the server, merge the value
# below into each generated map file, and start again.
#
# min-inhabited-time is a chunk's accumulated nearby-player time, in ticks,
# before BlueMap renders it. 30 ticks (~1.5 s) renders almost everything a player
# walked past; 1200 ticks (60 s) is a deliberate explored-terrain filter, so
# chunks a player only rushed through are left undrawn. The reference instance
# uses 1200: choose the value deliberately, and remember it needs a map
# re-render after any change. It is a map-render threshold, not an exact record
# of what a client saw, and it counts every chunk within a player's simulation
# distance. Leave any inhabited-time radius at its default. Minecraft
# view-distance is independent. See docs/bluemap.md.
min-inhabited-time: 1200
# TODO: keep the remaining generated map keys (name, world, dimension, storage,
# and any marker sets) from your BlueMap version. Static marker configuration
# stays administrator-managed; do not add marker-command addons to the plugin
# set. See https://bluemap.bluecolored.de/wiki/configs/Maps.html.
